    <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Process and Requirements","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>Listing occurs upon application by the issuer and must be submitted by a <a href=\"https://www.ser-ag.com/en/resources/recognized-representatives.html#/banks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Recognized Representative</a>. A bond is listed by using the web-based <a href=\"/content/six/global/en/products-services/the-swiss-stock-exchange/listing/connexor.html\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CONNEXOR</a> listing application. This allows a bond to enter into trading quickly and efficiently – provisional admission to trading can begin just three trading days from receipt of the electronic application. Subsequently, the issuer has two months to lodge a formal listing application, along with the required declarations and listing prospectus.</p>\r\n<p>Most relevant rules and regulations are:<br>\r\n- The <a href=\"https://www.ser-ag.com/dam/downloads/regulation/listing/listing-rules/lr-en.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Listing Rules</a><br>\r\n- The <a href=\"https://www.ser-ag.com/dam/downloads/regulation/listing/listing-rules/arb-en.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">Additional Rules for the Listing of Bonds</a><br>\r\n- The <a href=\"https://www.ser-ag.com/dam/downloads/regulation/listing/directives/dpds-en.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Directive on the Procedures for Debt Securities</a><br>\r\n- The <a href=\"https://www.ser-ag.com/dam/downloads/regulation/listing/admission-rules/RIB-en.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rules for the Admission of International Bonds to Trading on SIX Swiss Exchange</a></p>\r\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"New Admissions","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>Are you looking for recent and/or upcoming bond admissions on SIX Swiss Exchange? On SIX’s <a href=\"/content/six/global/en/market-data/bonds/admissions.html\">Recent and Upcoming Admission</a> website, you can look up respective bond(s).</p>\r\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where can I see the bond prospectus of a bond?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p><a href=\"https://www.ser-ag.com/en/resources/notifications-market-participants/prospectus-list.html#/\" target=\"_blank\">Prospectus list</a></p>\r\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Sustainable Bonds","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>Sustainable investments are needed to transform the economy and to deliver on climate, environmental and social sustainability goals, including the Paris Agreement and more broadly the UN Sustainable Development Goals.</p>\r\n<p>Bonds as a major asset class play an integral role to achieve such goals and the market for Green, Social, Sustainability or Sustainability-linked bonds is growing rapidly.</p>\r\n<p>To improve dissemination and awareness of sustainability factors and to facilitate investors’ search, a special flag (see “More filters”) has been introduced in the<a href=\"/content/six/global/en/market-data/bonds/bond-explorer.html\">&nbsp;Bond Explorer</a>&nbsp;that allows to filter either for&nbsp;<a href=\"/content/six/global/en/market-data/bonds/sustainable-bonds.html\">Green, Social, Sustainability or Sustainability-linked Bonds.</a></p>\r\n<p>For more information about sustainable bonds, please see <a href=\"/content/six/global/en/market-data/bonds/sustainable-bonds.html\">SIX’s Sustainable Bonds website</a>.&nbsp;</p>\r\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Bond Indices","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>SIX provides more than 300 different bond indices. The Swiss Bond Index (SBI) reflects the developments in the CHF-denominated bond market. The main SBI admission criteria are:<br>\r\n</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Size: At least CHF 100 million nominal amount per issuance</li>\r\n<li>Interest Rate: Straight bonds (fixed-rate notes) without additional clauses</li>\r\n<li>Tenor: Remaining term to maturity of at least one (1) year</li>\r\n<li>Rating: SBI “composite rating” (derived from the ratings of Standard &amp; Poor’s, Moody’s, Fitch and fedafin as well as those of major Swiss banks) of at least BBB</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Most relevant rules are:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The <a href=\"/content/dam/six/download/market-data/indices/bonds/six-methodology-sbi-index-rules-en.pdf\">Methodology Rulebook Governing Bond Indices</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>For more information about bond indices, please see <a href=\"/content/six/global/en/market-data/indices/bond-indices.html\">SIX’s Bond Indices</a> and <a href=\"/content/six/global/en/market-data/indices/esg-indices.html\">SIX’s ESG Indices</a> websites.</p>\r\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Bond Explorer","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>Are you looking for a bond being listed and/or traded on SIX Swiss Exchange? With <a href=\"/content/six/global/en/market-data/bonds/bond-explorer.html\">SIX’s Bond Explorer</a>, you can search for respective instrument(s). The Bond Explorer also provides pricing information, coupon information, maturity dates, currencies, etc. Any information can also be downloaded.</p>\r\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"In which languages can the listing documentation be submitted?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>All documents must be submitted in writing in either one of the following languages: German, French, Italian or English.</p>\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What information must be included in the listing prospectus?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>The listing prospectus is substantial to the entire process of the bond listing. It must include all relevant information about the issuer/company, the securities and where applicable, the guarantor. For detailed information of what information a bond listing prospectus must contain,<br>\r\nplease see&nbsp;<a rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.fedlex.admin.ch/eli/cc/2019/759/en\" target=\"_blank\">Ordinance on Financial Services</a>.</p>\r\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take for a bond to be listed and admitted to trading?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>The admission for provisional trading for bonds may be granted within three trading days after the related application is submitted with three additional trading days for a new issuer since in this case the submission of an application for pre-verification is required. The complete required listing documentation must be submitted within two months from the provisional admission to trading.</p>\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does the listing of a bond cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":""}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the main ongoing obligations that come with a bond listing?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>From the time at which securities are listed or admitted to trading on SIX, the issuer needs to fulfill certain obligations for maintaining a listing or admission to trading such as for example:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Financial reporting</li>\n<li>Ad hoc publicity</li>\n<li>Other reporting requirements regarding the issuer (e.g. change of company name, change of auditor, etc.) and the security (e.g. amortizations, early repayments, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><b>See also:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.ser-ag.com/en/resources/laws-regulations-determinations/regulations.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.ser-ag.com/en/resources/laws-regulations-determinations/regulations.html</a></b><br>\n</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Directive Regular Reporting Obligations (DRRO)<br>\n</li>\n<li>Directive on Financial Reporting (DFR)<br>\n</li>\n<li>Additional Rules for the Listing of Bonds (ARB)</li>\n</ul>\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will the bonds listed on SIX be directly admitted to the Swiss Bond Indices (SBI)?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>The Swiss Bond Indices (SBI) mirror the developments in the CHF-denominated bond market. Certain criteria must be met for a CHF bond to be admitted to the SBI:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Issue size: At least CHF 100 million.</li>\r\n<li>Bond categories: Only straight bonds (fixed-rate securities) without additional clauses. Exceptions to this rule are straight bonds subject to premature redemption, subordinated bonds and step-up bonds.</li>\r\n<li>Maturity: Remaining term to maturity of at least one year.</li>\r\n<li>Rating: Bonds must have a SBI composite rating of at least BBB*</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>* for more details click <a href=\"/content/dam/six/download/market-data/indices/index-regulation/market-consultations/six-market-consultation-sbi-rating-en.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</p>\r\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where can I see the bond prospectus of a bond?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p><a href=\"https://www.ser-ag.com/en/resources/notifications-market-participants/prospectus-list.html#/\" target=\"_blank\">Prospectus list</a></p>\r\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the minimum issuance amount for a bond listed and/or traded on SIX?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>The aggregated nominal value of a bond issue must be at least CHF 20 million (or an equivalent amount in another currency).</p>\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can the issuer submit the listing application himself?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>No, the issuer must appoint a <a href=\"https://www.ser-ag.com/en/resources/detail-information/recognized-representatives.html#/banks\" target=\"_blank\">Recognized Representative</a> to submit its listing application/documentation. The Recognized Representative assists and guides the issuer in respect of the admission to listing of its securities on SIX.</p>\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"In which currencies can a bond be listed and/or traded on SIX?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>Bonds denominated in all major world currencies can be listed and/or traded on SIX such as:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Australian Dollar (AUD)</li>\n<li>Canadian Dollar (CAD)</li>\n<li>Swiss Francs (CHF)</li>\n<li>Chinese Yuan Renminbi (CNY)</li>\n<li>Czech Krone (CZK)</li>\n<li>Danish Krone (DKK)</li>\n<li>Euro (EUR)</li>\n<li>British Pound (GBP)</li>\n<li>Hungarian Forint (HUF)</li>\n<li>Japanese Yen (JPY)</li>\n<li>Mexican Peso (MXN)</li>\n<li>Norwegian Krone (NOK)</li>\n<li>New Zealand Dollar (NZD)</li>\n<li>Polish Zloty (PLN)</li>\n<li>Russian Ruble (RUB)</li>\n<li>Swedish Krone (SEK)</li>\n<li>Turkish Lira (TRY)</li>\n<li>Singapore Dollar (SGD)</li>\n<li>US Dollar (USD)</li>\n<li>South African Rand (ZAR)<br>\n</li>\n</ul>\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What kinds of bonds can be listed and/or traded on SIX?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>Bonds listed and/or traded on SIX can be categorized as follows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Straight bonds</li>\n<li>Floating-rate bonds</li>\n<li>Convertible bonds</li>\n<li>Contingent convertibles</li>\n<li>Loan participation notes</li>\n<li>Subordinated bonds</li>\n<li>Dual-currency bonds</li>\n<li>Option bonds</li>\n<li>Zero bonds</li>\n</ul>\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it possible to list a financial instrument with a duration less than one year to maturity?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>Yes, it is. Financial instruments with a high liquidity and a maturity of less than one year are called &quot;Money Market Papers&quot;. The issuing and listing fees applied to Money Market Papers are lower than the other types of securities.</p>\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does an issuer have to exist to be able to list bonds on SIX?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<p>An issuer should have existed for at least three years (exemptions may be requested/granted). The financial statements of the last two full financial years must be included in the bond listing prospectus.</p>\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the main documents that need to be submitted along with the listing application?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"<ul>\n<li>The articles of association</li>\n<li>An excerpt from the Commercial Register (or any comparable foreign register) for a new issuer</li>\n<li>The listing prospectus</li>\n<li>The issuer declaration</li>\n<li>A copy of the certificate for permanent global certificates (if applicable)</li>\n<li>A copy of the register for uncertified securities (if applicable)</li>\n</ul>\n"}}]}</script>
    

