</section>
    </div>
<div class="section bg-light-gray section-z-bottom "  >
    <div class="bg"></div>
    <section>
      








    <h3 class="heading chapter_title ">Bond Listing At-a-Glance </h3>










    
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/etc.clientlibs/ihcc/components/content/container/accordion/clientlibs.min.ACSHASHc3254a3d67472fe62754ffbd32af0a2e.css" type="text/css">
<script src="/etc.clientlibs/ihcc/components/content/container/accordion/clientlibs.min.ACSHASH0c74b7ab3c4758e8267710172ab51b9c.js"></script>





<div>
    
    
    <div class="accordion" aria-multiselectable="false">
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="process-requirements" aria-expanded="false">Process and Requirements</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="process-requirements" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>Listing occurs upon application by the issuer and must be submitted by a <a href="https://www.ser-ag.com/en/resources/recognized-representatives.html#/banks" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Recognized Representative</a>. A bond is listed by using the web-based <a href="https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/the-swiss-stock-exchange/listing/connexor.html" target="_self" rel="noopener noreferrer">CONNEXOR</a> listing application. This allows a bond to enter into trading quickly and efficiently – provisional admission to trading can begin just three trading days from receipt of the electronic application. Subsequently, the issuer has two months to lodge a formal listing application, along with the required declarations and listing prospectus.</p>
<p>Most relevant rules and regulations are:<br> - The <a href="https://www.ser-ag.com/dam/downloads/regulation/listing/listing-rules/lr-en.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Listing Rules</a><br> - The <a href="https://www.ser-ag.com/dam/downloads/regulation/listing/listing-rules/arb-en.pdf" target="_blank" rel="nofollow">Additional Rules for the Listing of Bonds</a><br> - The <a href="https://www.ser-ag.com/dam/downloads/regulation/listing/directives/dpds-en.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Directive on the Procedures for Debt Securities</a><br> - The <a href="https://www.ser-ag.com/dam/downloads/regulation/listing/admission-rules/RIB-en.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Rules for the Admission of International Bonds to Trading on SIX Swiss Exchange</a></p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="sustainable-bonds" aria-expanded="false">Sustainable Bonds</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="sustainable-bonds" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>Sustainable investments are needed to transform the economy and to deliver on climate, environmental and social sustainability goals, including the Paris Agreement and more broadly the UN Sustainable Development Goals.</p>
<p>Bonds as a major asset class play an integral role to achieve such goals and the market for Green, Social, Sustainability or Sustainability-linked bonds is growing rapidly.</p>
<p>To improve dissemination and awareness of sustainability factors and to facilitate investors’ search, a special flag (see “More filters”) has been introduced in the<a href="https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/bonds/bond-explorer.html">&nbsp;Bond Explorer</a>&nbsp;that allows to filter either for&nbsp;<a href="https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/bonds/sustainable-bonds.html">Green, Social, Sustainability or Sustainability-linked Bonds.</a></p>
<p>For more information about sustainable bonds, please see <a href="https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/bonds/sustainable-bonds.html">SIX’s Sustainable Bonds website</a>.&nbsp;</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="bond-indices" aria-expanded="false">Bond Indices</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="bond-indices" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>SIX provides more than 300 different bond indices. The Swiss Bond Index (SBI) reflects the developments in the CHF-denominated bond market. The main SBI admission criteria are:<br></p>
<ul>
 <li>Size: At least CHF 100 million nominal amount per issuance</li>
 <li>Interest Rate: Straight bonds (fixed-rate notes) without additional clauses</li>
 <li>Tenor: Remaining term to maturity of at least one (1) year</li>
 <li>Rating: SBI “composite rating” (derived from the ratings of Standard &amp; Poor’s, Moody’s, Fitch and fedafin as well as those of major Swiss banks) of at least BBB</li>
</ul>
<p>Most relevant rules are:</p>
<ul>
 <li>The <a href="https://www.six-group.com/dam/download/market-data/indices/bonds/six-methodology-sbi-index-rules-en.pdf">Methodology Rulebook Governing Bond Indices</a></li>
</ul>
<p>For more information about bond indices, please see <a href="/content/six/global/en/market-data/indices/bond-indices.html">SIX’s Bond Indices</a> and <a href="/content/six/global/en/market-data/indices/esg-indices.html">SIX’s ESG Indices</a> websites.</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="bond-explorer" aria-expanded="false">Bond Explorer</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="bond-explorer" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>Are you looking for a bond being listed and/or traded on SIX Swiss Exchange? With <a href="https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/bonds/bond-explorer.html">SIX’s Bond Explorer</a>, you can search for respective instrument(s). The Bond Explorer also provides pricing information, coupon information, maturity dates, currencies, etc. Any information can also be downloaded.</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="new-admissions" aria-expanded="false">New Admissions</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="new-admissions" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>Are you looking for recent and/or upcoming bond admissions on SIX Swiss Exchange? On SIX’s <a href="https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/bonds/admissions.html">Recent and Upcoming Admission</a> website, you can look up respective bond(s).</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="prospectus-list-glance" aria-expanded="false">Where can I see the bond prospectus of a bond?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="prospectus-list-glance" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p><a href="https://www.ser-ag.com/en/resources/notifications-market-participants/prospectus-list.html#/" target="_blank">Prospectus list</a></p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
    </div>
</div>
</section>
    </div>
<div class="section section-z-top "  >
    <div class="bg"></div>
    <section>
      <div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <h4 class="paragraph_title">
                Frequently Asked Questions: Understanding Bond Listing and Trading on SIX</h4></div>
        </div>




    





<div>
    
    
    <div class="accordion" aria-multiselectable="false">
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="what_is_the_minimumissuanceamountforabondlistedandortradedonsix" aria-expanded="false">What is the minimum issuance amount for a bond listed and/or traded on SIX?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="what_is_the_minimumissuanceamountforabondlistedandortradedonsix" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>The aggregated nominal value of a bond issue must be at least CHF 20 million (or an equivalent amount in another currency).</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="in_which_currenciescanabondbelistedandortradedonsix" aria-expanded="false">In which currencies can a bond be listed and/or traded on SIX?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="in_which_currenciescanabondbelistedandortradedonsix" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>Bonds denominated in all major world currencies can be listed and/or traded on SIX such as:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Australian Dollar (AUD)</li>
 <li>Canadian Dollar (CAD)</li>
 <li>Swiss Francs (CHF)</li>
 <li>Chinese Yuan Renminbi (CNY)</li>
 <li>Czech Krone (CZK)</li>
 <li>Danish Krone (DKK)</li>
 <li>Euro (EUR)</li>
 <li>British Pound (GBP)</li>
 <li>Hungarian Forint (HUF)</li>
 <li>Japanese Yen (JPY)</li>
 <li>Mexican Peso (MXN)</li>
 <li>Norwegian Krone (NOK)</li>
 <li>New Zealand Dollar (NZD)</li>
 <li>Polish Zloty (PLN)</li>
 <li>Russian Ruble (RUB)</li>
 <li>Swedish Krone (SEK)</li>
 <li>Turkish Lira (TRY)</li>
 <li>Singapore Dollar (SGD)</li>
 <li>US Dollar (USD)</li>
 <li>South African Rand (ZAR)<br></li>
</ul></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="what_kinds_of_bondscanbelistedandortradedonsix" aria-expanded="false">What kinds of bonds can be listed and/or traded on SIX?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="what_kinds_of_bondscanbelistedandortradedonsix" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>Bonds listed and/or traded on SIX can be categorized as follows:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Straight bonds</li>
 <li>Floating-rate bonds</li>
 <li>Convertible bonds</li>
 <li>Contingent convertibles</li>
 <li>Loan participation notes</li>
 <li>Subordinated bonds</li>
 <li>Dual-currency bonds</li>
 <li>Option bonds</li>
 <li>Zero bonds</li>
</ul></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="is_it_possible_tolistafinancialinstrumentwithadurationlessthanon" aria-expanded="false">Is it possible to list a financial instrument with a duration less than one year to maturity?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="is_it_possible_tolistafinancialinstrumentwithadurationlessthanon" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>Yes, it is. Financial instruments with a high liquidity and a maturity of less than one year are called "Money Market Papers". The issuing and listing fees applied to Money Market Papers are lower than the other types of securities.</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="how_long_does_anissuerhavetoexisttobeabletolistbondsonsix" aria-expanded="false">How long does an issuer have to exist to be able to list bonds on SIX?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="how_long_does_anissuerhavetoexisttobeabletolistbondsonsix" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>An issuer should have existed for at least three years (exemptions may be requested/granted). The financial statements of the last two full financial years must be included in the bond listing prospectus.</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="can_the_issuer_submitthelistingapplicationhimself" aria-expanded="false">Can the issuer submit the listing application himself?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="can_the_issuer_submitthelistingapplicationhimself" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>No, the issuer must appoint a <a href="https://www.ser-ag.com/en/resources/detail-information/recognized-representatives.html#/banks" target="_blank">Recognized Representative</a> to submit its listing application/documentation. The Recognized Representative assists and guides the issuer in respect of the admission to listing of its securities on SIX.</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="what_are_the_maindocumentsthatneedtobesubmittedalongwiththelisti" aria-expanded="false">What are the main documents that need to be submitted along with the listing application?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="what_are_the_maindocumentsthatneedtobesubmittedalongwiththelisti" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><ul>
 <li>The articles of association</li>
 <li>An excerpt from the Commercial Register (or any comparable foreign register) for a new issuer</li>
 <li>The listing prospectus</li>
 <li>The issuer declaration</li>
 <li>A copy of the certificate for permanent global certificates (if applicable)</li>
 <li>A copy of the register for uncertified securities (if applicable)</li>
</ul></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="how_long_does_ittakeforabondtobelistedandadmittedtotrading" aria-expanded="false">How long does it take for a bond to be listed and admitted to trading?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="how_long_does_ittakeforabondtobelistedandadmittedtotrading" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>The admission for provisional trading for bonds may be granted within three trading days after the related application is submitted with three additional trading days for a new issuer since in this case the submission of an application for pre-verification is required. The complete required listing documentation must be submitted within two months from the provisional admission to trading.</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="in_which_languagescanthelistingdocumentationbesubmitted" aria-expanded="false">In which languages can the listing documentation be submitted?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="in_which_languagescanthelistingdocumentationbesubmitted" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>All documents must be submitted in writing in either one of the following languages: German, French, Italian or English.</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="what_informationmustbeincludedinthelistingprospectus" aria-expanded="false">What information must be included in the listing prospectus?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="what_informationmustbeincludedinthelistingprospectus" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>The listing prospectus is substantial to the entire process of the bond listing. It must include all relevant information about the issuer/company, the securities and where applicable, the guarantor. For detailed information of what information a bond listing prospectus must contain,<br> please see&nbsp;<a rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.fedlex.admin.ch/eli/cc/2019/759/en" target="_blank">Ordinance on Financial Services</a>.</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="what_are_the_mainongoingobligationsthatcomewithabondlisting" aria-expanded="false">What are the main ongoing obligations that come with a bond listing?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="what_are_the_mainongoingobligationsthatcomewithabondlisting" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>From the time at which securities are listed or admitted to trading on SIX, the issuer needs to fulfill certain obligations for maintaining a listing or admission to trading such as for example:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Financial reporting</li>
 <li>Ad hoc publicity</li>
 <li>Other reporting requirements regarding the issuer (e.g. change of company name, change of auditor, etc.) and the security (e.g. amortizations, early repayments, etc.)</li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><b>See also:&nbsp;<a href="https://www.ser-ag.com/en/resources/laws-regulations-determinations/regulations.html" target="_blank">https://www.ser-ag.com/en/resources/laws-regulations-determinations/regulations.html</a></b><br></p>
<ul>
 <li>Directive Regular Reporting Obligations (DRRO)<br></li>
 <li>Directive on Financial Reporting (DFR)<br></li>
 <li>Additional Rules for the Listing of Bonds (ARB)</li>
</ul></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="will_the_bonds_listedonsixbedirectlyadmittedtotheswissbondindice" aria-expanded="false">Will the bonds listed on SIX be directly admitted to the Swiss Bond Indices (SBI)?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="will_the_bonds_listedonsixbedirectlyadmittedtotheswissbondindice" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>The Swiss Bond Indices (SBI) mirror the developments in the CHF-denominated bond market. Certain criteria must be met for a CHF bond to be admitted to the SBI:</p>
<ul>
 <li>Issue size: At least CHF 100 million.</li>
 <li>Bond categories: Only straight bonds (fixed-rate securities) without additional clauses. Exceptions to this rule are straight bonds subject to premature redemption, subordinated bonds and step-up bonds.</li>
 <li>Maturity: Remaining term to maturity of at least one year.</li>
 <li>Rating: Bonds must have a SBI composite rating of at least BBB*</li>
</ul>
<p>* for more details click <a href="https://www.six-group.com/dam/download/market-data/indices/index-regulation/market-consultations/six-market-consultation-sbi-rating-en.pdf" target="_blank">here</a>.</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="how_much_does_thelistingofabondcost" aria-expanded="false">How much does the listing of a bond cost?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="how_much_does_thelistingofabondcost" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div class=table>
<div class="table-inner">
<table class="default fixed-row-column  "><thead><tr class="row1 odd     "><th class="     " >
                Single Bond Issuance</th><th class="     " >
                &nbsp;</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody><tr class="row2 even prominent    "><td class="     " >
                <b>Type of fee</b></td><td class="     " >
                <b>Amount</b></td></tr><tr class="row3 odd     "><td class="     " >
                Listing application fee</td><td class="     " >
                CHF&nbsp;2'500</td></tr><tr class="row4 even     "><td class="     " >
                Examination of the prospectus</td><td class="     " >
                CHF&nbsp;5'000</td></tr><tr class="row5 odd     "><td class="     "  valign="top">
                Variable fee based on size of issuance</td><td class="     " >
                1. “Variable fee for CHF-denominated bonds based on size of issuance” which is CHF 15 per CHF 1 million of nominal value<br>
2.&nbsp; “Variable fee for Non-CHF-denominated bonds based on size of issuance” which is CHF 10 per CHF 1 million of nominal value</td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>



<div class="spacer-v spacer-v--small "></div><div class=table>
<div class="table-inner">
<table class="default fixed-row-column  "><thead><tr class="row1 odd     "><th class="     " >
                Issuance Program</th><th class="     " >
                &nbsp;</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody><tr class="row2 even prominent    "><td class="     " >
                <b>Type of fee</b></td><td class="     " >
                <b>Amount</b></td></tr><tr class="row3 odd     "><td class="     " >
                Examination and registration of a program</td><td class="     " >
                CHF 6'000</td></tr><tr class="row4 even     "><td class="     " >
                Examination of the prospectus (in connection with the program)</td><td class="     " >
                CHF 2'000</td></tr><tr class="row5 odd     "><td class="     " >
                Reissuance (renewal) of issue program</td><td class="     " >
                CHF 3'000</td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    </div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="prospectus-list-faq" aria-expanded="false">Where can I see the bond prospectus of a bond?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="prospectus-list-faq" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p><a href="https://www.ser-ag.com/en/resources/notifications-market-participants/prospectus-list.html#/" target="_blank">Prospectus list</a></p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
    </div>
</div>
</section>
    </div>
<div class="section section-z-top " id="section-resources" >
    <span class=section-id id="resources"></span><div class="bg"></div>
    <section>
      


<div class="spacer-v spacer-v--large "></div>






    <h2 class="heading section_title ">Resources and Downloads</h2>













    





<div class="radio-tabs radio-tabs-active radio-tabs-compact" data-js-radio-tabs data-js-radio-tabs-scroll="true" data-js-radio-tabs-hash="true">
    
        <div class="tabs-scroll-left hidden">
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-link tabs-scroller-btn">
                <span class="fa fa-angle-left"></span><span class="sr-only">Scroll Left</span>
            </button>
        </div>
        <div class="radio-tabs-inner">
            
                <label class="radio-tabs-header ">
                    <input type="radio" name="tabs--2030792846" value="resources-service-information" checked/>
                    <span class="radio-tabs-element">Service Information</span>
                </label>
            
                <label class="radio-tabs-header ">
                    <input type="radio" name="tabs--2030792846" value="six-exchange-regulation"/>
                    <span class="radio-tabs-element">SIX Exchange Regulation</span>
                </label>
            
                <label class="radio-tabs-header ">
                    <input type="radio" name="tabs--2030792846" value="recognized-representatives"/>
                    <span class="radio-tabs-element">Recognized Representatives</span>
                </label>
            
        </div>
        <div class="tabs-scroll-right hidden">
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-link tabs-scroller-btn">
                <span class="fa fa-angle-right"></span><span class="sr-only">Scroll Right</span>
